  "Question": "How many subsets does the set \\(\\{1,2\\}\\) have in total?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A set with \\(n\\) elements has \\(2^n\\) subsets. A set with 2 elements has 4 subsets, including the empty set and the set itself.\n\nAlternative method 1: List every subset\n\nA subset can contain none, one, or both of the two elements. These possibilities give\n\\[\n\\varnothing,\\qquad \\{1\\},\\qquad \\{2\\},\\qquad \\{1,2\\}.\n\\]\nEvery subset is included because it must have zero, one, or two elements, and the four listed sets are distinct. Therefore there are \\(4\\) subsets.",
